{"event_id":"kimi-reopen:3","seq":3,"run_id":"kimi-reopen","session_id":"kimi-reopen","created_at":1789686775.863,"terminal":true,"type":"done","payload":{"status":"completed","last_seq":2,"result_summary":"approved: 3 finding(s)","review":{"schema_version":1,"verdict":"approved","risk":"read_only","markdown":"# Review\n\nAudited the G25 host-only contained-test reopening helper, shared identity validation, admission inspection port, and adversarial tests. All five criteria pass; no blocking defects. Ledger: action/admission/run identity and historical lease owner are validated together under BEGIN IMMEDIATE, expired lease permits inspection but is never stop proof, and held admissions stay held (asserted in every test). Binding: invocation ID derives solely from the exact action executionRef and is triangulated against canonical journal identity plus trusted manifest inputs; all ten substitution variants are rejected before daemon I/O. Authority: synchronous-only grants, cloned request/options/identity, and full fenced digest + journal rechecks across every await, with revocation/release/revision drift tested. Unknown: start is hard-denied, the recovery verifier unconditionally throws, no settle/release path is reachable, and lost DELETE ACK remains unknown without repeated deletion. Residual non-blocking gaps: conditional child-process coverage, untested concurrent double-stop race, and env-gated real-daemon tests.","judgments":[{"id":"ledger","pass":true,"severity":"error","summary":"inspectAdmission binds action generation, admission row owner, and historical lease owner under one immediate transaction with a full fence; expired lease enables inspection only, releasedAt!==null rejects reopen, and tests confirm admissions remain held."},{"id":"binding","pass":true,"severity":"error","summary":"Only the exact executionRef-derived invocation journal is used; canonical digest, realpath/O_NOFOLLOW, and per-field identity checks reject all tested substitutions before 